# ThreadSanitizer suppressions (TSAN_OPTIONS=suppressions=<this file>).
# Format: `race:<function or module substring>`, `mutex:`, `deadlock:`, `called_from_lib:<lib>`.
#
# Rules: dependency noise only, one justification line per entry; a race in
# first-party code is a bug to fix, never to suppress.
#
# Qt's own libraries are NOT built with TSan, so their internal synchronisation
# (lock-free QAtomic/QSharedData paths, QThreadStorage) is invisible to the tool
# and can produce false positives. If the first real TSan run shows them, prefer
# the narrowest suppression, e.g.:
#   Qt event dispatcher wakeup (glib) races reported without Qt's memory model:
#   called_from_lib:libQt6Core.so
# (called_from_lib silences EVERY report whose top frames are in that library;
#  use it only after confirming the reports are all false positives.)
#
# Empty until a real run proves otherwise.
